hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1351","Zakaria bin Yahya bin Aban and Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi Al-Misrian told us, they said: Ibn Abi told us Maryam, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Yazid bin Al Had told me, Shurahbil Abu Saad told me, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in the fear prayer: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and a group after the group that was behind the Messenger of God They all bowed their faces towards the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar.” So the two groups said “Allahu Akbar”, and he bowed, and the group behind him bowed, and the others were sitting, then he prostrated, so they prostrated also, and the others were sitting, then he stood up and they stood up, They sat down behind them until they were sitting in the place of their companions, and the other group came and he prayed one rak’ah and two prostrations with them, while the others were sitting, then He greeted, and both groups stood up and prayed for themselves one rak'ah and two prostrations, one rak'ah and two prostrations.\""
"
